--   The convergence half-plane of the ideal-counting Dirichlet series
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field with ring of integers $\mathcal O_K$, and write $N(I)=|\mathcal O_K/I|$ for the norm of a nonzero integral ideal. Let $a_K(n)$ count the nonzero integral ideals of norm $n$, and let $s\in\mathbb C$. Then
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\left|a_K(n)n^{-s}\right|<\infty\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\operatorname{Re}s>1.
--   $$
--
--   The ideal-counting Dirichlet series has the sharp absolute-convergence half-plane $\operatorname{Re}s>1$.
